The first cycle-2 run passed 332 tests, but the targeted rerun exposed a threaded signal case: SIGTERM can reach an unmasked worker thread and cause Python’s handler to run despite the main thread’s mask. I’ll also defer handler delivery during completion, then re-deliver the signal after the transaction records success.
